<task id="002" project="spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4">
  <metadata>
    <title>BFF matter/work-assignment event routes, per-record canCreate, delete-409 ProblemDetails (FR-08, FR-09)</title>
    <phase>1 Record template and actions</phase>
    <gate>startable after the owner reviews the plan and tasks (owner directive 2026-11-10)</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Tags bff-api, endpoints, authorization; adds external write routes (.cs)</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Authorization-sensitive write routes on the shared external-access surface (uac-r2, ebilling-r1)</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>A</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, endpoints, authorization, integration-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Add `POST /api/v1/external/{matters|workassignments}/{id}/events` by generalising the project event create over the root kind (as `CreateTodoForRoot` does), make the to-do, event and message lists tell every caller whether the matching create would be admitted (`canCreate`), and give the document-delete lock 409 the checkout 409's ProblemDetails `status`/`title` (#2271 residual).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in ASP.NET Core Minimal APIs, endpoint authorization on the external plane, and xUnit integration tests. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>The two event routes answer 201 for a caller with Create on that root and the event is regarding that root; the project route behaves exactly as before; list reads carry a `canCreate` that equals the create route's own decision; the delete 409 parses as ProblemDetails with `checkedOutBy`; contract, regression and arch tests pass; UAC's review is recorded.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-08, FR-09, FR-06. Event create is project-only; `ListEventsForRoot` returns `canCreate` only for a project (`ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs:2226-2229`); the to-do list only to `DataverseConfirmsWrites` callers (`:758-772`); the message list never. The documents list returns it to every caller (`:619-633`) — the model. #2271: the checkout 409 has `status`/`title` (`DocumentOperationsEndpoints.cs:158-177`); the delete 409 (`:497-500`) serialises the bare `DocumentLockedError`.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/WorkforceRoleCeilingGate.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ExternalDataService.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalMessageEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/DocumentOperationsEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/contract/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalRootEventCreateContractTests.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/regression/Issue2271_DeleteLockedDocumentProblemDetailsTests.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/DocumentDestroyAuthorizationTestFixture.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/integration/contract/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalMessageEndpointsTests.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/ExternalTodoScopeTests.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.Ledger.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/AuthenticationSchemeCensusTests.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Api/ExternalAccess/WorkforceCeilingRouteFamilyTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/contract/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalProjectEventContractTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/contract/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalRootEventReadTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-008 / FR-08">Both new routes are mapped in the same `/api/v1/external` group as the project route (inheriting `ExternalCollaboration` + `CallerPrincipalAuthorizationFilter`) and carry `.RequireWorkforceCeiling(...)` with new `CreateMatterEvent` / `CreateWorkAssignmentEvent` = `CreateChildUnder(MatterTable|WorkAssignmentTable, EventTable)` next to `CreateProjectEvent` (`WorkforceRoleCeilingGate.cs:124`), and the same `.Produces`/`.ProducesProblem` set as the project route.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-08">One handler `CreateEventForRoot(rootKind, …)` decides all three roots: `RightsForRootWriteAsync(… EventEndpoints.CreateEventPrivilege …)`, the 503 for an unanswered Dataverse question, the 403 `reasonCode = sdap.access.deny.insufficient_rights`, the 400 checks, `ResolveChildOwnerAsync` on the root's entity, and the creator stamp from the resolved principal. The parent comes only from the route; the request DTO gains no regarding member. The project route's responses (status, body, reasonCode, Location) do not change.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-08">`ExternalDataService.CreateEventAsync` / `BuildEventCreatePayload` (:2364, :2433) take the root kind and bind through `TryGetRootBinding(rootKind)` (:1571), as the to-do create does; never a client-supplied lookup.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-06 (enabler)">GET `/{projects|matters|workassignments}/{id}/todos`, `/{…}/events` and `/{root}/{id}/messages` return an additive `canCreate` to EVERY caller that equals the matching POST's own Create decision for that caller and record (no extra Dataverse read for a caller whose access Dataverse does not decide). Fields already sent keep their names and values. An unanswered Dataverse question reads as `canCreate: false`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-09 / ADR-019">The delete 409 in `DeleteDocument` (`DocumentOperationsEndpoints.cs:497-500`) returns `status = 409`, `title = "Document Locked"`, `error`, `detail`, `checkedOutBy`, `checkedOutAt`, `correlationId` — the exact shape of the checkout 409 (:165-177). `.Produces&lt;DocumentLockedError&gt;(409)` stays. No other delete outcome changes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="R3 gotcha">No DELETE route is added; `TheExternalPlane_MapsExactlyFourDeleteRoutes` stays green unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="bff-extensions">Placement Justification in the PR (cite `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`): extends existing external-access endpoints in place. Measure the publish-size delta against a fresh master build (report both sizes, the delta, the zip tool; ≤ 60 MB total; ≥ +5 MB needs justification). No new HIGH CVE (`dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`). No new DI registration, package or background work (NFR-05). Tests ship with every `Api/` and `Services/` change.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Run `/conflict-check` before opening the PR (shared surface with unified-access-control-r2 and ebilling-r1). Never deploy the dev BFF directly — task 018 requests the deploy through uac-r2 (`docs/procedures/dev-bff-deploy-coordination.md`). Build only on the net10 SDK.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-04">Logs and problem bodies added here carry no tenant, oid, UPN, email or token.</constraint>
  </constraints>

