  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load the knowledge files, read the relevant files, declare rigor and model tier per task-execute Step 0.5.</step>
    <step order="1">Add the two ceiling sets to `WorkforceRoleCeilingGate.cs`; map the two POST routes next to the project route.</step>
    <step order="2">Refactor `CreateEvent` into `CreateEventForRoot` with three thin adapters; parameterise `CreateEventAsync`/`BuildEventCreatePayload` by root kind.</step>
    <step order="3">Make the to-do, event and message list reads return `canCreate` per the FR-06 constraint.</step>
    <step order="4">Give the delete 409 the checkout 409's shape.</step>
    <step order="5">Write `ExternalRootEventCreateContractTests.cs` (theory over the two segments) for the route criteria below.</step>
    <step order="6">Extend the list tests (`ExternalTodoScopeTests.cs`, `ExternalMessageEndpointsTests.cs`, the new event file) for the `canCreate` criterion.</step>
    <step order="7">Write `Issue2271_DeleteLockedDocumentProblemDetailsTests.cs` on `DocumentDestroyAuthorizationTestFixture` (add a checked-out outcome to `RecordingCheckoutService`, :418).</step>
    <step order="8">Update the route ledger (`RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.Ledger.cs` HandlerDecision entries near :2091), `AuthenticationSchemeCensusTests.cs` (:117) and `WorkforceCeilingRouteFamilyTests.cs` (:82) for the two routes, with reasons.</step>
    <step order="9">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/`, `dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/` (re-run any host-timeout failures in isolation — R3 gotcha) and `dotnet test tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/`; measure publish size and CVEs; record both in the task notes.</step>
    <step order="10">Run `/conflict-check`; request UAC's review of the routes and the canCreate change (uac-r2 session) and record the outcome in the task notes and the PR.</step>
    <step order="11">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` and this POML's &lt;status&gt; to completed; run `pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1`.</step>
    <step order="12">Record deviations and decisions in `projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4/notes/task-002-notes.md`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If `sprk_event` has no regarding lookup for matter or work assignment under the binding `TryGetRootBinding` gives (the payload would need a different navigation property), STOP and escalate rather than inventing a binding.</trigger>
    <trigger>If returning `canCreate` on the message list needs more than the one rights probe the POST already performs, or would change any existing response field, STOP and escalate (UAC review).</trigger>
    <trigger>If UAC asks for a different authorization model for the new routes, STOP; do not merge until the owner decides.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the publish size passes 60 MB or a new HIGH CVE appears, STOP (bff-hygiene item 4/5).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>`POST /projects/{id}/events` (`ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs:456`, handler :2269); `CreateTodoForRoot` (:776); documents list `canCreate` (:633).</existing>
    <extension>Yes, and this task does it: the project handler is generalised; the two routes are thin adapters with ceilings from the existing `CreateChildUnder`; `canCreate` already exists on `ExternalCollectionResponse` (`ExternalProjectDtos.cs:38`).</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>"Add event" on a matter or work assignment has no route (404/405) although the caller holds Create, and the SPA cannot tell a partner's per-record right on matters, so FR-06's "no offered action answers 403" cannot be met.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test the BFF and ArchTests</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>

