  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Must fire: a caller with Create on a matter (and on a work assignment) POSTs an event and gets 201 with an `ExternalEventDto`; the Dataverse payload binds that root's regarding lookup and the root's owning team.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Must not fire: a View-only caller gets 403 with `reasonCode = sdap.access.deny.insufficient_rights` and nothing is written.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Must not fire: a record outside the caller's accessible set gets the same status the project route gives (403) and nothing is written.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Must not fire: a request without a valid external-plane bearer gets 401, as the project route does.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A missing `sprk_name` gets 400; an unanswered Dataverse rights question gets the retryable 503; a refused owner writes nothing — same bodies as the project route.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The project event route's existing contract tests pass unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">For matter and work assignment, the to-do, event and message lists return `canCreate: true` to a Create holder and `false` to a View-only holder, and in each case the matching POST answers 201 / 403 respectively.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The delete 409 body parses as ProblemDetails (status 409, title "Document Locked") and carries `checkedOutBy`, `checkedOutAt`, `error`, `detail` with unchanged names and shapes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The route ledger, the authentication-scheme census and the ceiling route-family tests list the two new routes; `TheExternalPlane_MapsExactlyFourDeleteRoutes` passes unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Build is green; BFF unit/integration tests and ArchTests pass; publish size (both sizes, delta, zip tool) is recorded and ≤ 60 MB; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">UAC's review of the new routes and the list `canCreate` change is recorded in the task notes and cited in the PR.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the must-fire/must-not-fire and edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-08, FR-09, FR-06, NFR-05, §Hot-Path Declaration. Copy the `CreateEvent_*` tests (`ExternalProjectEventContractTests.cs:177-225`, fixture `ExternalAccessContractFixture`). Anchors re-verified 2026-11-10: project POST map `:456`; GETs `:439/:447`; handler `:2269`; delete 409 `DocumentOperationsEndpoints.cs:497-500` (spec said ~494-498). The spec's FR-08 says "errorCode"; the project route's denials carry `reasonCode` — match whatever the project route sends, field for field. The `canCreate` widening is included here because FR-06 has no other server source for a partner's per-record right on matters and work assignments (`/me` lists project levels only — `bff-client.ts:170`). Two adversarial-review passes (authorization).</notes>

